          %h2#references References
          %p
            According to (
            %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, p. 131
            ) the notion of spectrum is due to
          %ul
            %li#Lima58
              E. L. Lima,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality and Postnikov invariants
          %blockquote
            %p
              It is generally supposed that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Whitehead"} G. W. Whitehead
              also had something to do with it, but the latter takes a modest attitude about that. (
              %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, p. 131
              )
          %p Early notes include
          %ul
            %li#Boardman65
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"}> Michael Boardman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable homotopy theory
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , Part III, section 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
          %p
            See the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1"} Introduction to stable homotopy theory – 1.1 Sequential Spectra
          %p More modern developments are due to
          %ul
            %li#LewisMaySteinberger86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Gaunce+Lewis"}> L. Gaunce Lewis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant stable homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/equi.pdf"} pdf
          %p The quick idea is surveyed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The stable homotopy category
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~carym/stable.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Mazel-Gee"}> Aaron Mazel-Gee
                ,
                %em An introduction to spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~aaron/writing/an-introduction-to-spectra.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The first review of stable homotopy theory with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            is (in terms of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-modules"} S-modules
          %ul
            %li#ElmendorfKrizMay95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Elmendorf"}> Anthony Elmendorf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Modern+foundations+for+stable+homotopy+theory"} Modern foundations for stable homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Elmendorf-Kriz-May/modern_foundations.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A comprehensive account of the symmetric model in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              %em Symmetric spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            and in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Global+homotopy+theory"} Global homotopy theory
              (take
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F} = \{1\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant stable homotopy theory
              to plain stable homotopy theory).
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Thomason"}> Robert Thomason
                ,
                %em Symmetric Monoidal Categories Model All Connective Spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.37.8193"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Infinite loop spaces
            %li#Ayoub
              %p
